title: SPlit.jl
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the
  metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jongsu Liam
    family-names: Kim
    email: jongsukim8@gmail.com
repository-code: https://github.com/appleparan/SPlit.jl
url: https://liam.kim/SPlit.jl
abstract: >-
  Distribution-preserving subset selection for tabular data and
  embeddings: optimal train/test splits, k-fold multiplets, and
  training-data selection by support points, kernel herding, twinning,
  and kernel thinning. Available for Julia (SPlit.jl) and Python (splitiq).
keywords:
  - data splitting
  - subset selection
  - support points
  - energy distance
  - maximum mean discrepancy
  - kernel thinning
  - julia
  - python
